WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.194
Today is November 03, 2026.

3
00:00:07.194 --> 00:00:10.540
Overnight, the Dow rose against the tide.

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.625
The S&P 500 and Nasdaq gave up early gains and closed lower.

5
00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:21.790
The Nasdaq fell 1.07 percent to 25,164.

6
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:27.954
The S&P 500 lost 0.51 percent, or about 39 points.

7
00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:33.567
The S&P has now closed below its half-year moving average for two straight sessions.

8
00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:40.123
Money kept rotating out of technology and into insurance, healthcare, credit and internet retail.

9
00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:44.241
The ten-year Treasury yield slid back below 5 percent.

10
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:48.040
Some money leaving the AI trade went into bonds.

11
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.552
Oil fell along with yields.

12
00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:56.128
But the VIX climbed as high as 21.7, and that ended the intraday rebound.

13
00:00:56.128 --> 00:00:58.775
Iran drove the drop in oil.

14
00:00:58.775 --> 00:01:04.792
Before the open, Tehran offered a phased plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz within days.

15
00:01:04.792 --> 00:01:10.969
Secretary of State Rubio said President Trump prefers diplomacy and is holding off on new strikes.

16
00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:17.611
By the afternoon, Iranian media said messages had passed through intermediaries, with no progress.

17
00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:21.900
The talks have not broken down, so crude held its losses.

18
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.172
But Iran's core demands have not changed.

19
00:01:25.172 --> 00:01:28.763
The risk is that strikes resume after the midterms.

20
00:01:28.763 --> 00:01:31.716
If they do, oil could jump again.

21
00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:35.993
The midterm election is today, and results are expected tonight.

22
00:01:35.993 --> 00:01:40.969
Prediction markets give Democrats a 94 percent chance of taking the House.

23
00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:44.045
They give 75 percent for the Senate.

24
00:01:44.045 --> 00:01:47.819
Bulls say divided government brings policy stability.

25
00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:52.047
Bears warn that tax cuts and deregulation could be reversed.

26
00:01:52.047 --> 00:01:54.486
History favors the bulls.

27
00:01:54.486 --> 00:02:00.160
The S&P 500 has risen in the twelve months after every midterm since 1950.

28
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.290
The average gain has been roughly 14 to 15 percent.

29
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.709
Still, the election is a secondary driver.

30
00:02:07.709 --> 00:02:11.361
Monetary policy and earnings decide the direction.

31
00:02:11.361 --> 00:02:15.650
On the Fed, the debate is about rate hikes, not cuts.

32
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.711
CME futures put the odds of a December rate hike at 72 percent.

33
00:02:20.711 --> 00:02:23.456
The economy is still running warm.

34
00:02:23.456 --> 00:02:28.309
The ISM manufacturing index rose to 55.5.

35
00:02:28.309 --> 00:02:31.275
That is ten straight months of expansion.

36
00:02:31.275 --> 00:02:34.277
This week's jobs data matters a lot.

37
00:02:34.277 --> 00:02:40.773
The ADP report comes Wednesday, with 65,000 to 85,000 jobs expected.

38
00:02:40.773 --> 00:02:47.304
Friday's payrolls are expected near 70,000, with unemployment steady at 4.2 percent.

39
00:02:47.304 --> 00:02:52.917
With the labor market near full employment, inflation will decide what happens in December.

40
00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:57.746
The Fear and Greed Index sits at 23, which is extreme fear.

41
00:02:57.746 --> 00:03:00.748
That is not a capitulation signal yet.

42
00:03:00.748 --> 00:03:05.834
Past bottoms reached 3 on Liberation Day and 6 during the Iran war.

43
00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:11.618
Q-Q-Q failed at 700 and now sits near its 250-day moving average.

44
00:03:11.618 --> 00:03:16.434
If that line breaks, the next level to watch is near 660.

45
00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:23.150
On the Nasdaq Composite, watch 25,000 and the annual line near 24,700.

46
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:29.081
For the S&P 500, the bearish downside target is near 7,200.

47
00:03:29.081 --> 00:03:33.971
In the past, breaks of the annual line have paid off for patient buyers.

48
00:03:33.971 --> 00:03:36.900
But history does not repeat on schedule.

49
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.964
The selling is centered on AI hardware.

50
00:03:39.964 --> 00:03:46.434
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index dropped 3.4 percent to 10,328.

51
00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.167
Just below sits 10,000.

52
00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:54.057
The annual line, a round number and a Fibonacci level all meet there.

53
00:03:54.057 --> 00:03:57.268
A bounce from that zone would not be surprising.

54
00:03:57.268 --> 00:04:02.035
Until chips stabilize, the broader correction is unlikely to end.

55
00:04:02.035 --> 00:04:04.339
Demand is not the problem.

56
00:04:04.339 --> 00:04:11.434
South Korea's October chip exports jumped 259 percent to 56.4 billion dollars.

57
00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:17.133
Even so, foreign investors kept selling Korean chip names like SK Hynix.

58
00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:20.699
The real worry is the cost of the AI buildout.

59
00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:28.469
Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle cut buybacks by 83 percent in the first three quarters.

60
00:04:28.469 --> 00:04:33.873
That is down from 81.8 billion to 13.6 billion dollars.

61
00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:37.047
It is the lowest in at least fifteen years.

62
00:04:37.047 --> 00:04:39.633
Instead, they are borrowing.

63
00:04:39.633 --> 00:04:43.076
Alphabet plans a six billion euro bond.

64
00:04:43.076 --> 00:04:48.591
Meta is weighing at least 20 billion dollars in debt across the dollar and euro markets.

65
00:04:48.591 --> 00:04:57.047
Off-balance-sheet commitments at the hyperscalers, Nvidia, Broadcom and SpaceX now total 4.11 trillion dollars.

66
00:04:57.047 --> 00:05:00.429
People owned the megacaps as cash machines.

67
00:05:00.429 --> 00:05:04.608
That case is weakening, and investors are losing patience.

68
00:05:04.608 --> 00:05:10.589
On the other side, White House adviser Kevin Hassett says AI funding remains plentiful.

69
00:05:10.589 --> 00:05:13.652
He sees no risk of a broad selloff.

70
00:05:13.652 --> 00:05:18.358
Bill Ackman is buying the dip in Amazon, Meta and Microsoft.

71
00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.931
The biggest deal shock came in optical networking.

72
00:05:21.881 --> 00:05:28.499
Marvell agreed to buy Lumentum in an all-stock deal, at 4.5 Marvell shares per Lumentum share.

73
00:05:28.499 --> 00:05:32.800
Lumentum holders will own 33 percent of the combined company.

74
00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.624
The deal is expected to close in early 2028.

75
00:05:36.624 --> 00:05:38.965
There is no cash premium.

76
00:05:38.965 --> 00:05:42.371
Lumentum fell 18.6 percent.

77
00:05:42.371 --> 00:05:47.261
Marvell fell 12.7 percent and broke below its annual line.

78
00:05:47.261 --> 00:05:49.614
The strategy makes sense.

79
00:05:49.614 --> 00:05:54.933
Marvell needs Lumentum's indium phosphide lasers to complete its optical platform.

80
00:05:54.933 --> 00:06:00.178
Management expects more than 1.1 billion dollars a year in cost savings.

81
00:06:00.178 --> 00:06:06.317
But two richly valued stocks are being marked down together, and Chinese approval is uncertain.

82
00:06:06.317 --> 00:06:12.151
Lumentum's revenue rose 136 percent, and even that could not stop the slide.

83
00:06:12.151 --> 00:06:15.031
Palantir beat on every major line.

84
00:06:15.031 --> 00:06:19.847
Revenue jumped 96 percent to 2.31 billion dollars.

85
00:06:19.847 --> 00:06:24.749
For the first time, U.S. commercial revenue was larger than government revenue.

86
00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:28.266
Fourth quarter guidance came in above forecasts.

87
00:06:28.266 --> 00:06:32.947
Still, the stock slipped after hours on weak short-term momentum.

88
00:06:32.947 --> 00:06:37.653
Four stocks have clear signals today: two buys and two sells.

89
00:06:37.653 --> 00:06:40.141
Nvidia is the first buy.

90
00:06:40.141 --> 00:06:44.798
Among the five leading chip stocks, it has the largest market cap.

91
00:06:44.798 --> 00:06:48.768
It also has the lowest valuation and the strongest growth.

92
00:06:48.768 --> 00:06:53.229
At nearly five trillion dollars, it will not rise tenfold.

93
00:06:53.229 --> 00:06:56.170
But its moat makes it steadier than most.

94
00:06:56.170 --> 00:07:00.264
Buy around 203 dollars, near the current price.

95
00:07:00.264 --> 00:07:04.332
Add if it breaks below 199 dollar support.

96
00:07:04.332 --> 00:07:08.205
Your risk gauge is the chip index holding 10,000.

97
00:07:08.205 --> 00:07:13.241
Berkshire Hathaway B shares are the defensive buy, but only on a pullback.

98
00:07:13.241 --> 00:07:17.764
They hit a record high in October, while many stocks nearly halved.

99
00:07:17.764 --> 00:07:21.403
They also rose during the 2022 bear market.

100
00:07:21.403 --> 00:07:27.911
Cash and Treasury bills totaled 365.5 billion dollars at the end of the second quarter.

101
00:07:27.911 --> 00:07:34.455
Over five years, the stock returned about 92 percent, beating all three major indexes.

102
00:07:34.455 --> 00:07:36.624
Do not chase the record.

103
00:07:36.624 --> 00:07:40.227
Start buying near 530 dollar support.

104
00:07:40.227 --> 00:07:43.180
Add near 512 dollars.

105
00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:47.335
This is a position to build steadily and hold for the long term.

106
00:07:47.335 --> 00:07:49.957
Apple is a take-profits signal.

107
00:07:49.957 --> 00:07:56.844
Fiscal fourth quarter revenue reached about 114.5 billion dollars, up 12 percent.

108
00:07:56.844 --> 00:08:02.077
Earnings per share were 2.10 dollars, above the 2.00 dollar estimate.

109
00:08:02.077 --> 00:08:05.031
iPhone and Mac sales both beat.

110
00:08:05.031 --> 00:08:08.597
But five cents of that came from tariff refunds.

111
00:08:08.597 --> 00:08:14.749
Without them, gross margin was about 46.9 percent, below expectations.

112
00:08:14.749 --> 00:08:19.994
Greater China revenue missed, and iPad and wearables also disappointed.

113
00:08:19.994 --> 00:08:23.511
The stock fell about 3 percent after hours.

114
00:08:23.511 --> 00:08:28.768
Investors seeking safety pushed Apple up about 25 percent from its June low.

115
00:08:28.768 --> 00:08:35.055
It now trades near 39 times forward earnings, roughly double the S&P 500.

116
00:08:35.055 --> 00:08:41.979
The average analyst target is 332 dollars, below the recent price near 338.

117
00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:46.195
Sell into any bounce back toward 338 dollars.

118
00:08:46.195 --> 00:08:51.207
If Apple keeps sliding, the market loses one of its usual stabilizers.

119
00:08:51.207 --> 00:08:53.229
Oracle is the sell.

120
00:08:53.229 --> 00:08:58.560
Five days after its investor day, Oracle broke its own financing promise.

121
00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.891
It had pledged no more than 20 billion dollars in new funding through fiscal 2030.

122
00:09:03.891 --> 00:09:09.516
Now it is raising the full 20 billion at once, half in stock and half in bonds.

123
00:09:09.516 --> 00:09:13.707
Long-term debt is near 117 billion dollars.

124
00:09:13.707 --> 00:09:19.381
Free cash flow is expected at negative 23.7 billion dollars this year.

125
00:09:19.381 --> 00:09:25.570
S&P Global Ratings already rates Oracle B-B-B minus, one notch above junk.

126
00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:29.614
Another downgrade would force investment-grade funds to sell.

127
00:09:29.614 --> 00:09:33.634
Credit default swap prices have spiked several times.

128
00:09:33.634 --> 00:09:36.955
Key support is 114 dollars.

129
00:09:36.955 --> 00:09:40.656
A break there opens a path toward 100 dollars.

130
00:09:40.656 --> 00:09:43.290
Use rallies to cut exposure.

131
00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:48.131
At best, Oracle is a short-term trade, not a long-term hold.

132
00:09:48.131 --> 00:09:56.305
Key events this week are tonight's midterm results, AMD earnings, Wednesday's ADP report, and Friday's payrolls.

133
00:09:56.305 --> 00:09:58.438
Keep cash on hand.

134
00:09:58.438 --> 00:10:01.612
Buy at your levels, not on headlines.

135
00:10:01.612 --> 00:10:05.619
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

136
00:10:05.619 --> 00:10:09.786
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
